FIX FE VIEW-STATISTICS SCREEN (821): reconstruct View_Statistics @0x44d300 + 3 setup thunks

The Information button's "View Statistics" record (Info nested table @0x469b78 rec-0 ACTION
0x44d300) drilled into an interactive stats-category viewer that was never decompiled by
Ghidra (below the game-code selection threshold) -> its VA sat in the dispatch as a raw
address and trapped on wasm (call_indirect to an unregistered VA). The screen dispatches a
category descriptor table @0x468050 (stride 0x14: +0 pos.word, +4 setup-fn, +8 render-fn)
whose SETUP slots hold three trivial label-thunks (0x44d4e8 Driver / 0x44d508 Track /
0x44d528 Championship) that were likewise unregistered raw VAs -> even after the main fn was
callable, `call [0x468054]` (cat-0 setup) would call_indirect an unrelocated VA.

Reconstructed 1:1 from objdump of dd2h.exe:
- View_Statistics @0x44d300..0x44d4e6: the category loop. Pad-nav bits match the other FE
  viewers (0x80/0x20 = prev/next category via byte tables 0x468088/0x46808a, 0x4000 =
  drill-in, 0x1000 = exit). Renders (View_Driver/Track/Champ_Stats) + all helpers
  (Rotate_Slab_On, Draw_All flip, Setup_Screen_Text/Lines, Button_Pressed, ...) already
  exist+registered. Typed int(void) to match the nested `code`=int() dispatch.
- Setup thunks 0x44d4e8/0x44d508/0x44d528: label-setters (write the category's string VA to
  slots 0x468020 + 0x468034, then Setup_Screen_Text(0x467fe8)). cat-2 uses two distinct
  strings (0x46d88c title / 0x46d8ac body) per the asm.

All 4 registered in dd2_dispatch.c so dd2_relocate rewrites the descriptor + nested-table VAs
to real table indices. This DISPROVES the prior "toolchain call_indirect bug" hypothesis: the
screen trapped only because its handlers were unregistered raw VAs, not a binaryen anomaly.
Unreconstructed-thunk + int-typing class (patches 770/816/817/818).

